# EVERY WORKSPACE ROOT NEEDS ITS OWN LINE.
#
# `/target` is ANCHORED to the repository root, so it covers exactly one
# workspace and no other. Each additional workspace root brings its own
# `target/` that this line does not reach — and an unignored one is not a small
# mistake: `kit-build/target` reached 830 MB / 2996 files within an hour of the
# workspace existing, all of it staged by a plain `git add -A` into a repository
# being prepared for public release.
#
# This has now happened twice. `brine-tests/target` was caught by hand at stage
# time when that workspace landed; `kit-build/target` was caught by a reviewer.
# Neither was caught by a rule. If you add a fourth workspace root, add its line
# HERE, in the same commit.
/target
/brine-tests/target
/kit-build/target
/dist

# CI pipeline params files (contain inline secrets — never commit)
ci/pipelines/*.params.yml

.claude/worktrees/

# Per-deployment telemetry salt (generated; never commit a salt)
.telemetry-salt
__pycache__/

# vitest failure screenshots — local run artifacts, never committed
kit/app/frontend/.vitest-attachments/
